# Settings for github.com/grafana/dashboard-linter.
exclusions:
  target-instance-rule:
    reason: >
      Service-level dashboard for an HPA-managed deployment (1-10 pods with
      churning pod names). Queries deliberately aggregate across instances
      and are scoped by the namespace/job template variables instead; a
      per-instance selector would break aggregation during scale events
      and rollouts.
  template-instance-rule:
    reason: >
      Same rationale as target-instance-rule: pods are ephemeral under HPA,
      so an instance variable would pin queries to dead pods. Per-pod
      breakdowns that matter (runtime, ECPDS cache size) group by the pod
      label instead.
  target-rate-interval-rule:
    reason: >
      aviso_sse_connection_duration_seconds is only observed when SSE
      connections close, which is sparse (connections live up to hours).
      A fixed 30m window keeps the histogram quantiles stable; the default
      $__rate_interval (~40s at common ranges) would mostly return no data.
